# Banked evidence: large, and fully reproducible from public no-auth endpoints.
# Keeping it out of git history is deliberate — the round-2 series probe alone
# banks ~800 events / ~15k markets (hundreds of MB), and every byte of it can be
# refetched. What must be version-controlled is the CODE and the
# PRE-REGISTRATIONS, because those are what the evidence is judged against.
#
#   tapes/       <- python3 fetch_tapes.py          (earnings / armed events)
#                <- python3 probe_series.py --fetch (the series probe)
#   book-tapes/  <- ./record-book.sh                 NOT reproducible: the Kalshi
#                   order book has no historical API. If one of these matters,
#                   copy it somewhere durable rather than relying on this tree.
#   out/*.json   <- regenerated by the scorers from tapes/. probe-result.json
#                   alone is 4.6 MB. The .md SCOREBOARDS in out/ are kept —
#                   those are conclusions, not intermediates.
tapes/
book-tapes/
out/*.json
out/*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ...EXCEPT these two, which are NOT regenerable and must be versioned.
#
#   probe-result.json  is the output of a ONE-SHOT measurement that
#                      PRE-REGISTRATION-R2-PROBE.md §P4 forbids re-running. "It
#                      can be regenerated from tapes/" is false: regenerating it
#                      IS the second scoring pass the pre-registration rules out.
#                      4.5 MB is a small price for the only copy of a result that
#                      cannot legitimately be recreated.
#   probe-roster.json  is the DECLARED POPULATION and the ordering witness — its
#                      immutable `generated_utc` is what proves no event entered
#                      the population because of anything seen in its own tape
#                      (defect D1 already cost us the other half of that proof).
!out/probe-result.json
!out/probe-roster.json
